  eatTip: "Lunch is the cheap meal here: smørrebrød and the traditional dishes are lunch things, and most classic Danish places close at 16–17. Dinner for a group is where Copenhagen gets expensive — do street food (Broens, Reffen), Kødbyen, or Absalon's 65-kr communal dinner. Tap water is free and excellent — ask for <b>postevand</b>. No tipping expected; round up if you liked it.",

