  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- INFO ----
  info: {
    sections: [
      { title: "Getting around", items: [
        "<b>Walk.</b> The centre is 3 km across and flat; every line here is designed to be done on foot.",
        "<b>Metro</b> (M1–M4) runs 24/7, driverless, every 2–6 min. <b>Harbour buses</b> 991/992 are normal buses that float — same ticket.",
        "<b>Tickets:</b> Rejsebillet app (replaced DOT Billetter in 2025) or the machines. 2 zones 24 kr, 3 zones 30 kr. Airport ↔ centre = 3 zones. DTU = 3–4 zones (≈30–38 kr).",
        "<b>Never walk in the bike lanes</b> — the ones with the little kerb. Look both ways before stepping off any pavement; bikes come from behind.",
        "Locals wait for the green man even at 3 am. Do the same.",
        "Taxis are ≈300–350 kr airport → centre. The metro is 30 kr and faster.",
      ] },
      { title: "Airport ↔ city", items: [
        "<b>Metro M2</b> from inside Terminal 3 to Kongens Nytorv (15 min) or Nørreport (17 min). Trains every 4–6 min, also at night.",
        "<b>Regional trains</b> from Terminal 3 to Central Station (13 min) if the hotel is near Tivoli/Vesterbro.",
        "3-zone ticket, 30 kr, from the red machines or the Rejsebillet app. Validate nothing — just carry it.",
        "Be at the airport <b>90 min before</b> a Schengen flight with bags, 60 without.",
      ] },
      { title: "Money", items: [
        "Danish kroner (DKK). Roughly <b>7.45 kr = 1 €</b>; 100 kr ≈ 13 €.",
        "Cards and Apple/Google Pay everywhere, including hot-dog carts. Many places are card-only. You don't need cash except maybe in Christiania.",
        "No tipping culture — service is in the price. Rounding up 5–10% for great service is appreciated, never expected.",
        "<b>Pant:</b> cans and bottles carry a 1–3 kr deposit; supermarkets have return machines.",
      ] },
      { title: "This week specifically", items: [
        "<b>Sunset ≈19:00</b>, sunrise ≈07:10. Daylight until about 19:30.",
        "<b>Tivoli</b>: summer season ends in late September, Halloween opens 2 October — check tivoli.dk for the exact days. The Food Hall is open all year.",
        "<b>Sunday:</b> big shops in the centre open 11–17; museums and sights open as normal.",
        "<b>Monday:</b> most museums are closed (Glyptotek, Designmuseum, Thorvaldsens, SMK, Christiansborg tower, Cisternerne). Supermarkets, bakeries and sights like the Round Tower are open.",
        "<b>Reffen</b> and <b>Broens Gadekøkken</b> are at the end of their seasons — check their sites the day before.",
      ] },
      { title: "Weather & what to bring", items: [
        "Late September: <b>10–16 °C</b>, windy, showers that pass. Layers, a rain jacket with a hood (umbrellas lose to the wind), shoes you can do 6 km in.",
        "A tote bag for supermarket beers and pastries. A power bank — the map is your compass.",
        "Plugs are the two-pin European type (C/F fit; the Danish K socket also takes them).",
      ] },
      { title: "Safety & health", items: [
        "Very safe city. Watch bags in Nyhavn crowds and on the metro, that's about it.",
        "<b>112</b> for emergencies. <b>1813</b> is the medical helpline to call before going to an emergency room.",
        "Pharmacies are called <b>Apotek</b>; Steno Apotek at Central Station is open 24 h.",
        "Tap water is excellent — ask for <b>postevand</b> in restaurants and it's free.",
      ] },
      { title: "How Danes are", items: [
        "Quiet in public, direct in conversation, punctual to the minute. 'Hej' for hello, 'hej hej' for goodbye.",
        "Everyone speaks English. A 'tak' (thanks) goes a long way anyway.",
        "Queues are sacred; so is personal space on the bus.",
        "Hygge is real: candles on café tables at noon, nobody rushing you out.",
      ] },
    ],
    phrases: [
      ["Hej / Hej hej", "Hi / Bye"],
      ["Tak", "Thanks"],
      ["Tak for mad", "Thanks for the meal"],
      ["Skål!", "Cheers!"],
      ["Undskyld", "Sorry / excuse me"],
      ["Ja / Nej", "Yes / No"],
      ["En øl, tak", "A beer, please"],
      ["Postevand", "Tap water"],
      ["Hvor er…?", "Where is…?"],
      ["Tillykke!", "Congratulations!"],
    ],
  },
